high-margin consumable revenue. Its growth engine is clinical diagnostics (oncology, hereditary disease, MRD), while research/academic markets are weak. It is expanding into proteomics (SomaLogic), spatial biology (StrataMap Spatial), and data monetization (Billion Cell Atlas). Understandability: HIGH.\n\n2-2. Moat score (0\u20133 each)\n- Intangible assets (brand, patents, reference databases): 3\n- Switching costs (workflow validation, data pipelines): 3\n- Network effects (genome data, partner ecosystem): 2\n- Cost advantage (scale manufacturing): 2\n- Economies of scale: 2\n- Regulatory barriers (IVD approvals): 2\n- Data moat: 2\nTotal: 16/21 \u2192 FORTRESS.\nMoat direction: Intangibles NARROWING (patent cliffs, Element/MGI/ONT competition) [Estimate]; data/network WIDENING (Billion Cell Atlas) [Estimate]; switching cost STABLE. Net: STABLE, with one compression vector.\n\n2-3. Lynch classification\nFAST GROWER transitioning toward STALWART. Overall revenue growth is only 6\u20139%, but clinical segment is growing mid-teens [Estimate]. Key checkpoint: ensure earnings growth (not just clinical volume) is durable; research demand is currently a net drag (\u22127% research consumables YoY) [Estimate - transcript].\n\n2-4. Financial strength scorecard\n- Revenue: FY22 $4.526B \u2192 FY25 $4.343B \u2192 TTM $4.494B; 3-yr CAGR \u22121.4% [Actual]; Trailing 4Q YoY trend: +5.0%, +4.8%, +9.4% [Actual - pack].\n- Operating margin: FY25 18.6% GAAP (median 12-yr 18.2%) [Actual]; TTM 18.6% [Actual].\n- EPS: FY25 $5.45 (diluted) [Arithmetic]; FY26 non-GAAP EPS guide $5.30\u2013$5.40 [Estimate - company].\n- ROE: 32.3% trailing per vendor [Estimate]; ROIC below WACC on adjusted basis (Layer 2.5) [Assumption].\n- FCF margin: $0.931B / $4.494B = 20.7% [Arithmetic/Actual].\n- Net debt (T0): cash + ST investments $1.17B vs total debt $1.99B at Q2'26 \u2192 net debt $0.82B [Estimate - company call]; adding operating leases $0.56B \u2192 $1.38B [Estimate]. Net debt/EBITDA \u2248 1