enario | Prob | Final Rev 2035 ($B) | Term Op Margin | WACC/g | IV/share |\n|----------|------|---------------------|----------------|--------|----------|\n| Bear | 25% | 5.2 (CAGR 1.2%) | 17% | 11.75%/2.5% | $38 |\n| Base | 50% | 7.2 (CAGR 5.7%) | 25% | 11.25%/3.0% | $83 |\n| Bull | 25% | 8.8 (CAGR 8.4%) | 27% | 10.50%/3.25% | $117 |\n\nBayesian note: Prior base rate for re-acceleration ~40\u201350%; posterior Base probability increased to 50% after Q2'26 guidance raise and clinical demand evidence [Estimate]. No further update triggers available beyond Q3/Q4 filings.\nExpected price = 0.25\u00d738 + 0.50\u00d783 + 0.25\u00d7117 = $80 [Arithmetic/Assumption]. 50% CI: $60\u2013$105. 80% CI: $38\u2013$125.\nMargin of Safety vs $219.40: (83 \u2212 219.40)/83 = \u2212164% \u2192 NONE.\n\nSECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- Market-implied horizon: To justify $219, the market must be discounting roughly 10+ years of strong execution with FCFF growing 14\u201316% annually to ~$3.5B by 2035 (reverse DCF, WACC 11.25%) [Arithmetic/Assumption].\n- My horizon: 3\u20135 years. In 3\u20135 years, realistic price from base case \u2248 $95\u2013$120.\n- Spread > 5 years: this is a genuine horizon-arbitrage SIGNS, but in the direction of AVOID, not buy.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500-\nConviction score (0\u20133 each, total 15):\n1. Business quality: 2 (fortress moat, but moat compression vector and mixed financial record)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0 (price >2.6x high-end IV)\n3. Macro alignment: 1 (headwind)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3 (KPI-rich: clinical consumables growth, X conversion, gross margin)\n5. Execution traceability: 1 (guidance raised, but FY25 revenue declined and Q1'26 miss)\nTotal: 7/15 \u2192 MEDIUM. Conviction decay: \u22121 every 6 months without confirming evidence.\nSizing: Max weight for fresh long at Medium conviction = 0% because valuation fails MoS (>30% required). Long only if price \u2264 $120 (MoS 31%). Exit/trim rules in Section 8.\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- Short interest: 9.46% of float; 4.25 days to cover; MoM change \u22124.9% [Actual - but 15 days stale]. Short covering during a rising clinical narrative is a momentum tailwind, not an edge.\n- Institutional ownership: 1.08% [Unconfirmed \u2014 implausible; excluded from analysis].\n- Options/sentiment: price above 52-week high after +~100% 12-month move [Estimate]; put/call skew data not held [Unconfirmed].\n- Crowding risk score: 11/15 (new high, AI/genomics narrative, momentum, short-covering). Per framework: reduce position size by \u22121pt \u2014 irrelevant for a no-position rating.\n- Consensus: sell-side mean PT $195.83 (stale 8/10) [Estimate]; our IV is well below even the lowest PT $113 [Estimate], which itself is above our bear case. This widens the credibility gap: consensus multiples are anchored, not discounted.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- High-beta (1.46), long-duration cash flows, rate-sensitive, USD-weakness beneficiary, China-export-exposed.\n- It is a poor fit for defensive or income portfolios. For aggressive growth sleeves it offers optionality but at a punitive entry price.\n- Correlation with Nasdaq high-beta/semis is 0.6\u20130.7 [Assumption]; in a stagflationary shock (top regime, 35%), ILMN is likely to underperform with high drawdown (>50% plausible) [Assumption].\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nFor a LONG at $219.40:\nExpected long payoff = $80 \u2212 $219.40 = \u2212$139.40/share \u2192 Kelly fraction = 0% (negative edge) [Arithmetic].\nTheoretical short Kelly (using bear/base/bull at 25/50/25 and a forced $300 stop = loss of $80.60, win of $181.40):\np_win \u2248 0.55, p_loss \u2248 0.45, b = 181.40/80.60 = 2.25; Kelly \u2248 (0.55\u00d72.25 \u2212 0.45)/2.25 = 35% \u2014 but this is theoretical and DANGEROUS in a crowded squeeze; after 50% confidence haircut and cap for Engine 3/shorting prohibitions: 0% [Assumption]. Layer 5 (0%) vs Layer 6.5 (0%) \u2014 gap 0pp; no re-analysis required.\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nRisks:\n- China unreliable-entity-list ban (Feb 2025) [Actual], China \u22487% of revenue pre-ban, six consecutive quarters of decline [Estimate - MedTech Dive]. Bear-case tail risk if ex-China clinical stalls.\n- Competitive pricing from Element/MGI/ONT [Estimate].\n- SBC dilution: 0.275B/yr = 33% of reported FCF [Actual].\n- Research funding caution (7% YoY decline in research consumables) [Estimate - transcript].\n- Key-person/activist distraction: Covax reduced stake [Estimate].\nCatalysts:\n- Clinical consumables +15% ex-China; US-Canada +20%+ [Estimate - transcript].\n- NovaSeq X conversion target 80\u201385% by end-2026 [Estimate - transcript].\n- Billion Cell Atlas: 300M cells, 6 biopharma partners [Estimate - transcript].\n- FY26 revenue guide raised to $4.60\u2013$4.64B; non-GAAP EPS $5.30\u2013$5.40 [Actual - company press release].\n- Possible China UEL resolution [Unconfirmed].\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n- Stressed-correlation profile (2008/2020/2022 analog): ILMN trades like high-beta tech; in a liquidity event, 10Y rises and HY spreads widen simultaneously \u2014 ILMN suffers both duration compression and funding-flow risk [Assumption].\n- CVaR (95%): model implies ~45\u201355% drawdown under the Bear regime; likely 12-month tail loss of ~$100/share from $219 [Assumption].\n- Portfolio-level rule: do not combine ILMN with more than 5% exposure to long-duration high-beta healthcare/life-science tools; diversify with shorter-duration cash-generative positions in the same sleeve.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLong-trigger thresholds (all must be met):\n- Price \u2264 $120 (MoS \u2265 31% vs base IV) [Assumption].\n- Q3/Q4 2026 clinical consumables growth ex-China \u2265 10% YoY.\n- FY26 non-GAAP operating margin \u2265 23% (vs ~22.5% Q2).\n- GAAP operating margin (excluding impairments) \u2265 20% for 2 consecutive quarters.\n- Net debt/EBITDA \u2264 1.5x.\nHold/trim thresholds if already long:\n- Trim if price > $230 without a corresponding IV increase.\n- Sell/exit if clinical consumables growth < 5% for two quarters OR if China revenue falls to ~0 and is not offset elsewhere.\n- Re-evaluate if Element/MGI platform wins a >15% share of a major U.S. clinical account [Unconfirmed].\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n9-1. Short thesis (same data):\n1) True distributable FCF is only ~$0.66B after SBC, 